I think it'd be *generally* safer to the do nesting check here, since that guarantees that it cannot be missed if any future changes are made to this method; hence something like this (which also removes the need to manually increment the counter in the call below):
```javascript
    if (++nestingCounter > MAX_NESTING) {
      warn("Visibility expression is too deeply nested");
      return;
    }
```
